<title>UK: BOC stake in Japan OSK to rise to 49.67 pct.</title>
<headline>BOC stake in Japan OSK to rise to 49.67 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>BOC Group Plc said on Wednesday that it was converting the bonds it held in Japanese industrial gases company Osaka Sanso Kogyo KK (OSK) into 40.3 million new shares.</p>
<p>The conversion would hike BOC's holding in OSK from a current 25.47 percent to 49.67 percent.  </p>
<p>BOC acquired the bonds in 1982. The conversion would not require any additional funds, BOC said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
